---
/**
 * One turn as `runTurn` (inside `kernelTurns`) runs it: the steps, each one model call and the tool calls its answer
 * asks for, and the ways a turn ends, with the closing call at the step cap, after a spend refusal, and the harvest.
 */
import Figure from "./Figure.astro"
---

<Figure label="The loop inside a turn" minWidth={760}>
  <svg class="rv-svg" viewBox="0 0 900 560" role="img" aria-labelledby="tl-t">
    <title id="tl-t">A turn: open a session, then each step asks the model once and runs the calls its answer asks for, until it answers in words, gives its verdict, or reaches its step cap</title>
    <defs>
      <marker id="tl-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path class="head" d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z"></path></marker>
      <marker id="tl-b" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path class="head-accent" d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z"></path></marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- start -->
    <rect class="core" x="40" y="14" width="360" height="66" rx="10"></rect>
    <text x="56" y="38" class="t-b">Open the turn</text>
    <text x="56" y="56" class="t-xs t-dim">a session in the turn's journal (its turns recovered first);</text>
    <text x="56" y="71" class="t-xs t-dim">the tail stored as its first message; the closing reserve kept back</text>
    <path class="line" d="M220 80 V108" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>

    <!-- the step -->
    <rect class="zone" x="20" y="112" width="560" height="296" rx="14"></rect>
    <text x="36" y="134" class="t-mono t-sm t-accent">step n   (n ≤ the step cap)</text>
    <rect class="box" x="40" y="146" width="360" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
    <text x="56" y="166" class="t-sm"><tspan class="t-mono">memory.context(session)</tspan></text>
    <text x="56" y="184" class="t-xs t-dim">the journal as messages: append-only</text>
    <path class="line" d="M220 194 V214" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>
    <rect class="model" x="40" y="218" width="360" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
    <text x="56" y="240" class="t-sm"><tspan class="t-mono">modelAnswer</tspan>: one model call</text>
    <text x="56" y="258" class="t-xs t-dim">prefix + context, all six tools offered; held, then settled on the ledger</text>
    <path class="line" d="M220 274 V294" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>
    <rect class="box-2" x="40" y="298" width="360" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
    <text x="56" y="318" class="t-sm">Does the answer ask for tool calls?</text>
    <text x="56" y="334" class="t-xs t-dim">(an answer cut at the output cap runs its calls, then ends)</text>
    <path class="line" d="M220 342 V362" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>
    <text x="230" y="358" class="t-xs t-dim">yes</text>
    <rect class="box" x="40" y="366" width="360" height="34" rx="8"></rect>
    <text x="56" y="388" class="t-sm"><tspan class="t-mono">callTool</tspan> for each: its result stored</text>
    <path class="line-accent" d="M40 383 H28 V170 H38" marker-end="url(#tl-b)"></path>
    <text x="410" y="388" class="t-xs t-accent">↺ then the next step</text>

    <!-- no calls -->
    <path class="line" d="M400 320 H612" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>
    <text x="440" y="314" class="t-xs t-dim">no: it answered in words</text>
    <rect class="box" x="616" y="226" width="270" height="140" rx="10"></rect>
    <text x="630" y="248" class="t-b t-sm">Answered in words</text>
    <text x="630" y="270" class="t-xs t-dim">a finder turn: one harvest call, its</text>
    <text x="630" y="286" class="t-xs t-dim">host's note asks it to report what it</text>
    <text x="630" y="302" class="t-xs t-dim">weighed and kept to itself</text>
    <text x="630" y="326" class="t-xs t-dim">a check: one closing call asking for its</text>
    <text x="630" y="342" class="t-xs t-dim">verdict (a verdict in text is not counted)</text>
    <text x="630" y="358" class="t-mono t-xs t-core">→ Answered · Judged</text>

    <!-- verdict -->
    <path class="line" d="M580 156 H612" stroke-dasharray="3 4" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>
    <rect class="box" x="616" y="112" width="270" height="88" rx="10"></rect>
    <text x="630" y="134" class="t-b t-sm">A check's verdict recorded</text>
    <text x="630" y="156" class="t-xs t-dim">checked after every step's calls:</text>
    <text x="630" y="172" class="t-xs t-dim">the check ends at once</text>
    <text x="630" y="190" class="t-mono t-xs t-core">→ Judged</text>

    <!-- step cap -->
    <path class="line" d="M300 408 V436" marker-end="url(#tl-a)"></path>
    <text x="310" y="428" class="t-xs t-dim">the step cap, or a refusal with the reserve held</text>
    <rect class="core" x="40" y="440" width="560" height="104" rx="10"></rect>
    <text x="56" y="462" class="t-b t-sm">The closing call</text>
    <text x="56" y="482" class="t-xs t-dim">the reserve released · the host's note stored (step cap note, or the harvest note)</text>
    <text x="56" y="498" class="t-xs t-dim">one more call with the same six tools offered, so the cached prefix holds;</text>
    <text x="56" y="514" class="t-xs t-dim">only its reporting calls run (reportFinding, or verdict), asked once more when the</text>
    <text x="56" y="530" class="t-xs t-dim">tool refused one: at most two calls · <tspan class="t-mono t-core">→ StepCap · Judged · SpendRefused</tspan></text>

    <!-- failures -->
    <rect class="danger" x="616" y="390" width="270" height="154" rx="10"></rect>
    <text x="630" y="412" class="t-b t-sm t-danger">Stops with the findings so far</text>
    <text x="630" y="434" class="t-xs t-dim">the ledger refuses a call · SpendRefused</text>
    <text x="630" y="452" class="t-xs t-dim">a call fails · ModelFailed</text>
    <text x="630" y="470" class="t-xs t-dim">an answer cut at the output cap · OutputCut</text>
    <text x="630" y="488" class="t-xs t-dim">the journal fails · JournalFailed</text>
    <text x="630" y="512" class="t-xs t-dim">it never fails the review: how it</text>
    <text x="630" y="528" class="t-xs t-dim">ended is part of its result</text>
  </svg>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <strong>A turn is the host's loop on the kernel.</strong> Each <strong>step</strong> is one model call; the tool
    calls its answer asks for run in that step. The kernel stores every answer and result in the turn's journal, and
    the next step's context is read back from it. The first call of a group's turn, or of the first turn of a whole
    review, is asked once more after a failure worth another try (a rate limit, a provider's error, a lost connection).
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
